factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 5 problems
  Reel script says the TN income tax raid was on the lorry owner's home and office 'நேற்று' (yesterday), which is consistent; however the reel_script states the 'தி மு க ஆட்சிக் காலத்தில்' sentence attributes the lorry supply to the DMK era, which matches the article, so no issue there; but the slides_spec 'பின்னணி' slide and the reel_script both say the raids concerned Senthil Balaji-linked places, which the article only describes as places 'said to be' linked, and the reel_script omits that qualifier
  Reel script says the raids were carried out by 'வருமான வரித்துறை அதிகாரிகள்' only, while the article says the Enforcement Directorate (அமலாக்கத்துறை) also conducted raids at various places; the reel_script's Senthil Balaji paragraph does mention this, but the slides_spec 'என்ன சோதனை?' slide wrongly ties the raid solely to Income Tax officers
  The caption describes Senthil Balaji-linked places as having been raided by Income Tax and Enforcement officials, which slightly conflates the 'said to be linked' places with the Sachidanandam raid, mixing two facts into one sentence
  The reel_script says the raid was 'டாஸ்மாக் முறைகேடு வழக்கு தொடர்பாக' and that officials said it is in progress, but the article says officials only said the search is 'taking place' in connection with the case; the reel_script's statement that Sachidanandam was supplying alcohol bottles from distilleries is a fair reading, but the slides_spec 'லாரி உரிமையாளர் ... மதுபாட்டில் விநியோக ஒப்பந்ததாரராகச் செயல்பட்டவர்' is present in the article, so no invented fact there
  The slides_spec and reel_script do not mention that the article's report covers searches 'at various places' in addition to the lorry owner's premises, which is an omission of context but not a central fact
